# W3 native-save bisection  -  win-x64, 2026-11-17

Goal: find why the installed desktop's project-memory native save
cancels (DownloadItem `done` -> interrupted, 0 bytes written) after a
completed UIA-driven Save-As dialog.

Bisection (idle sidecar children, same packaged asar, driver-driven):
- idle child, stdio ['pipe','pipe','pipe'] + Node IPC channel: FAIL
- idle child, stdin 'ignore', stdout/stderr pipes, stdout handshake: PASS
=> initial conclusion: the Node `stdio:'ipc'` channel cancels the download.

Fix attempt: replaced the parent<->backend Node IPC channel with
newline-JSON frames ('HARNESS_IPC ' prefix) over stdin/stdout pipes
(apps/desktop/backend-policy.ts attachBackendStdioChannel /
backendChannelSend / requestBackendShutdown; apps/server/main.ts
stdio channel; main.ts stdio ['pipe','pipe','pipe']; shutdown test
rewritten). Typecheck/lint/unit(4/4)/package all green.

Verify (verify-installed-desktop --project-memory-retention, real
packaged build): STILL FAILS identically ("the native save was
interrupted or its byte count changed", nativeSave.dialog.status=
running, 0 bytes). The stdin pipe alone did not fix it.

Discriminating control run: same fix packaged with stdio
['ignore','pipe','pipe'] + HARNESS_BACKEND_STDIN=0 (backend skips
stdin listeners -> no child-side channel at all):
  .harness-release-output-stdin0c -> verify run-1794930564447-*:
  FAILS IDENTICALLY (dialog.status=running, byte check fails).

Conclusion: REFUTED. Neither the Node IPC channel nor the stdin pipe
explains the cancel. The real backend fails with ANY stdio shape,
while the idle child passed with the same shapes -> the earlier
idle-child bisection was confounded (n=1 cells); the discriminating
factor is inside the real backend or harness environment, not the
channel. Probable next suspects (not yet bisected): the backend's
listening HTTP server / uv-loop activity, its env, or UIA/CDP
interplay in the harness driver.

Transport change reverted entirely (no proven benefit; do not ship an
unproven rework of a launch-token custody channel). Status: FAIL,
root cause deeper than the channel  -  recorded honestly.
